    <description>Quickly create a new opportunity off a contact record or get called from completing an event

2026-08-20: Restrict Stage picklist to open stages only (INC3-51)
2026-09-14: AP - accountLevelSelector&#39;s choice order swapped so Practice renders first, matching it already being the default-selected value (was previously a mismatch between what&#39;s selected and what&#39;s shown first).
2026-10-13: AP - OPS-356: Alerts Christina (Slack U0968T9RLF7) in the inventory channel (C09QW96BBTP) when a customer success user creates an Expansion opportunity (Scanner Upgrade or New Scanner). After Set_Account_Level the flow now goes to Is_Expansion_Opportunity (new) instead of straight to Upgrading_Scanners; Expansion + role starting with CS -&gt; Get_Organization_Info -&gt; Is_Sandbox_Org (sandboxes skip the post, same stop gap as CS Handover) -&gt; Get_Opp_Account -&gt; Expansion_Opportunity_Slack_Message -&gt; Upgrading_Scanners. Everything else continues to Upgrading_Scanners as before. Nothing removed.
2026-10-14: AP - OPS-356: Fixed opportunities created from a Contact getting the New Sales record type when Scanner Upgrade or New Scanner was selected (the record type formula read the default Type, which is &quot;New Sale&quot; from a Contact). recordTypeIdForOpportunity now returns the Expansion record type when Expansion_Type is Scanner Upgrade or New Scanner; otherwise it behaves as before. Nothing removed.
2026-10-15: AP: Added Exchange to the Expansion Type dropdown. Exchange writes Type = Exchange on the opportunity (opportunityType), uses the Expansion record type (recordTypeIdForOpportunity) and names the opportunity with Exchange (Name formula) so an exchange can be told apart from a Scanner Upgrade. Nothing removed.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <description>Put on the parent account if it exists AND this person&#39;s account doesn&#39;t have a practice id; fall back to inputAccount when called without a contact</description>
        <name>accountForOpportunity</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(
  NOT(ISBLANK({!recordId.Id})),
  IF(
    NOT(ISBLANK({!recordId.Account.Practice_ID__c})),
    {!recordId.AccountId},
    IF(
      NOT(ISBLANK({!recordId.Account.ParentId})),
      {!recordId.Account.ParentId},
      {!recordId.AccountId}
    )
  ),
  {!inputAccount.Id}
)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>The account the Opportunity is created on, after the rep has chosen a level. Practice means the contact&#39;s own account, never the parent. Corporate falls through to accountForOpportunity, which is unchanged.</description>
        <name>accountForOpportunityFinal</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(
  {!accountLevelSelector} = &quot;Practice&quot;,
  {!contactAccountId},
  IF(
    NOT(ISBLANK({!corporateAccountId})),
    {!corporateAccountId},
    {!contactAccountId}
  )
)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>The contact&#39;s own account - or the passed-in account when the flow is launched without a contact.</description>
        <name>contactAccountId</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(
  NOT(ISBLANK({!recordId.Id})),
  {!recordId.AccountId},
  {!inputAccount.Id}
)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>The corporate account above the contact&#39;s account. Prefers Corporate_Parent_Account__c over ParentId - it is the dedicated pointer, the New Account button stamps it on every practice it creates, and it is marginally more complete in production (681 populated versus 678). Blank when there is no corp above, which is the B3 case.</description>
        <name>corporateAccountId</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(
  NOT(ISBLANK({!recordId.Account.Corporate_Parent_Account__c})),
  {!recordId.Account.Corporate_Parent_Account__c},
  IF(
    NOT(ISBLANK({!recordId.Account.ParentId})),
    {!recordId.Account.ParentId},
    &quot;&quot;
  )
)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>The corporate account&#39;s NAME, for naming a corporate-level opportunity. This is a three-hop traversal and everything else this flow reads is two hops, so runtime population is unproven - the cascade ends at the contact&#39;s own account name, which is today&#39;s behaviour, so the worst case is no improvement rather than a wrong name.</description>
        <name>corporateAccountName</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(
  NOT(ISBLANK({!recordId.Account.Corporate_Parent_Account__r.Name})),
  {!recordId.Account.Corporate_Parent_Account__r.Name},
  IF(
    NOT(ISBLANK({!recordId.Account.Parent.Name})),
    {!recordId.Account.Parent.Name},
    {!recordId.Account.Name}
  )
)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>The Account Level radio&#39;s starting value: whatever the account is already classified as, otherwise Practice. The fallback changed from Corporate on 2026-09-08 - 78% of existing corporate-level opportunities touch exactly one practice and only 3% touch more than one, so the old default was wrong most of the time. NOTE this means accepting the default no longer reproduces pre-Account_Level__c behaviour: it now creates a practice-level opportunity and stamps the account Practice.</description>
        <name>defaultAccountLevel</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(
  NOT(ISBLANK({!recordId.Id})),
  IF(
    ISBLANK(TEXT({!recordId.Account.Account_Level__c})),
    &quot;Practice&quot;,
    TEXT({!recordId.Account.Account_Level__c})
  ),
  IF(
    ISBLANK(TEXT({!inputAccount.Account_Level__c})),
    &quot;Practice&quot;,
    TEXT({!inputAccount.Account_Level__c})
  )
)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>defaultCloseDate</name>
        <dataType>Date</dataType>
        <expression>TODAY() + 30</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>Names the opportunity after the account it will actually be created on, not after the contact&#39;s account. Those diverge for a practice contact choosing Corporate - a case that produced 19 production opportunities named after one of their corp&#39;s own children. The rep can still edit the name on screen 2.</description>
        <name>defaultName</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(
  NOT(ISBLANK({!recordId.Id})),
  IF(
    {!accountLevelSelector} = &quot;Practice&quot;,
    {!recordId.Account.Name},
    {!corporateAccountName}
  ),
  {!inputAccount.Name}
) &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; 
IF(
{!Expansion_Type}={!Scanner_Upgrade},&quot;Scanner Upgrade&quot;,
IF( {!Expansion_Type} = {!New_Scanner},&quot;New Scanner&quot;,
IF( {!Expansion_Type} = {!Exchange},&quot;Exchange&quot;,
&quot;New Sale&quot;)))
 &amp; &quot; - &quot; &amp; TEXT({!$Flow.CurrentDate})</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>defaultOpportunityType</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(NOT(ISBLANK({!recordId.Id})), &quot;New Sale&quot;, &quot;Expansion&quot;)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>OPS-356. Link to the new opportunity for the Slack message, built the same way CS Handover builds its Onboarding link.</description>
        <name>newOpportunityLink</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>LEFT({!$Api.Partner_Server_URL_260}, FIND(&#39;/services&#39;, {!$Api.Partner_Server_URL_260}) - 1) &amp; &#39;/lightning/r/Opportunity/&#39; &amp; {!newOpp.Id} &amp; &#39;/view&#39;</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>opportunityType</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(
{!Expansion_Type}={!Scanner_Upgrade},&quot;Scanner Upgrade&quot;,
IF( {!Expansion_Type} = {!New_Scanner},&quot;New Scanner&quot;,
IF( {!Expansion_Type} = {!Exchange},&quot;Exchange&quot;,
&quot;New Business&quot;)))</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>Expansion record type when the rep picked Scanner Upgrade or New Scanner on the screen, so launching from a Contact no longer gives New Sales. Otherwise falls back to the default Type: New Sales from a Contact, Expansion from an Account.</description>
        <name>recordTypeIdForOpportunity</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(OR({!Expansion_Type}={!Scanner_Upgrade}, {!Expansion_Type}={!New_Scanner}, {!Expansion_Type}={!Exchange}), {!expansionRecordTypeID}, IF(ISPICKVAL({!newOpp.Type}, &quot;New Sale&quot;), {!newSalesRecordTypeID}, {!expansionRecordTypeID}))</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>statusChangeNote</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&quot;Upsell opportunity created by &quot; &amp; {!$User.FirstName} &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp; {!$User.LastName} &amp; &quot; on &quot; &amp; TEXT({!$Flow.CurrentDate})</expression>
    </formulas>
